# Success notices

After an explicit save, edit, assign, confirm, or delete, show a success modal. Reuse `useNotice`, `NoticeLayer`, and `NoticeDialog` from `@/shared/ui`. Do not copy overlay markup or add a second toast.

- Keep the button as the action verb (`Save`, `Assign`). Do not change it to «Сохранили» / `Saved`.
- Title: `common.savedNotice` or a short action-specific line. Hint only if it clarifies.
- Skip live typing, chips, theme/language, and binary toggles that persist immediately.
- If a form closes after save, show the modal on the screen the user lands on.

```tsx
const { notice, show, hide } = useNotice()
show(t('common.savedNotice'), t('today.saved'))
<NoticeLayer notice={notice} onClose={hide} />
```
